Stephanie

Rather than focus upon differences between the contrasting pieces of software. I think the telling point is your next-to-last statement: data that you provide in your figure isn't great.  It doesn't appear from the histogram that detectability is influenced by distance from the transect.  I would be surprised that the half normal has an AIC close to the AIC for the uniform.  I don't expect the adjustment terms are having any influence upon the shape of the detection function; hence "pretty much identical AIC values".

There isn't a model being fitted when using a uniform key without adjustments; it is effectively a strip transect.  So density is simply number detected divided by area covered by the sampling effort.

Happy to discuss off-list if you want to discuss.
